      "message": "accelgryo_bmi_common.c is also used by CONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI220 and CONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI3XX.\n\nHowever, I don\u0027t understand why this check is needed.  For cros-ec builds, this module is already guarded by the necessary configs:\ndriver/build.mk\n```\ndriver-$(CONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI160)+\u003daccelgyro_bmi160.o accelgyro_bmi_common.o\ndriver-$(CONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI220)+\u003daccelgyro_bmi260.o accelgyro_bmi_common.o\ndriver-$(CONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI260)+\u003daccelgyro_bmi260.o accelgyro_bmi_common.o\ndriver-$(CONFIG_ACCELGYRO_BMI3XX)+\u003daccelgyro_bmi3xx.o accelgyro_bmi_common.o\n```\n\nAnd for Zephyr EC builds, CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ACCELGYRO_BMI is a helper symbol that cannot explicitly get enabled. Instead the user enables the driver symbol (such as CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ACCELGYRO_BMI3XX) which does a `select PLATFORM_EC_ACCELGYRO_BMI`.",
